Description: Resolve document portal paths before looking for a removable drive
 In a sandboxed installation the file dialog goes through
 xdg-desktop-portal, because GTK routes GtkFileChooserNative there whenever
 it finds /run/flatpak-info, and that cannot be turned off. The portal
 reports the chosen file under the document portal, so exporting to a USB
 stick yields /run/user/1000/doc/<doc id>/print.bgcode instead of
 /run/media/<user>/<label>/print.bgcode. The file is the same one, the
 document portal passes writes through, but the path no longer has the
 mount point in it, so is_path_on_removable_drive finds no drive and the
 finished export notification comes up without its Eject button, which is
 the only way left to eject a drive from the application. Asks the document
 portal for the path the document stands for. Of its two methods for this,
 only GetHostPaths can be called from inside a sandbox; Info answers "Not
 allowed in sandbox".
 The call is made with a one second timeout rather than the 25 seconds
 libdbus defaults to, since it happens on the main thread, and its result
 is kept. Paths outside the document portal cost no call.
